y  metabolomix perhaps  genomics rna-seq  very systems biology methods and i think  the future is how to  integrate these and pull them together  so that you can get a better bigger  picture  of what is going on in in  toxicology that you're seeing  so one thing you will notice is during  the presentation i didn't go into a lot  of details  about high content analysis itself  and a lot of the background and how to  do it and things like that  the reason for that is because this is  actually just one of a series  of webinars and a lot of that in  information  uh basic concepts on high throughput  screening and and  and uh high content analysis will be  dealt in some of these webinars that are  coming up  so there'll be one here by uh josh  harrell who was mentioned  during my presentation and also mark  anthony bray who was involved in  the development of cell painting uh  he'll be giving one and then later on  there'll be another one on  on 3d 3d models for drug discovery  so i would highly recommend that you get  on over  to the the lab roots website and  register for these ones because  together all of these will give you a  very nice package of  information on on high content analysis  for various different applications  and so finally i'd like to thank sbi 2  for the chance to  help out with this it's always extremely  enjoyable to work with sbi 2.  you should definitely check out the sbi  2 website and  have a look at the the annual meeting  hopefully next year that we'll be able  to do that  live again also i'd like to thank victor  wong at core life analytics  who was an enormous help in pulling  together all the information for this  and liz rubitsky who  was also very helpful liz works  in safety at drug safety at pfizer  and she was great help in in helping us  to figure out what we should be  presenting here  and uh liz should always also should  also be available  hopefully for to help out with some of  your answers to some of  the questions and so with 